        "file": "globber.py",
        "claim": "The `doublestar` matcher consumes `/` as an empty segment in several branches, allowing patterns such as `a/**/b` to match paths with consecutive slashes like `a//b`. The docstring describes whole path segments, not empty segments.",
        "severity": "medium",
        "status": "dropped",
        "investigation": "no deterministic repro; dropped (not repaired)"
      },
      {
        "id": "doublestar-alone-segment-consumption",
        "file": "globber.py",
        "claim": "For a standalone `**` token, the matcher consumes a segment by advancing to the next `/` and then recursing on the same `**` token without explicitly requiring the separator. This can accept malformed segment boundaries and empty segments in ways not specified by the docstring.",
